# Secrets for the Office Town worker.
#
# Cloudflare's "Deploy to Cloudflare" button reads this file and surfaces
# each variable as a form field. ALL four are optional — the worker boots
# fine with every field blank. Set any of them post-deploy via
# `wrangler secret put NAME` if/when you need them.

# OPTIONAL — gates the HTTP API + all 6 MCP servers.
# Leave blank to let the worker auto-generate one on first request
# (it's stored in D1 worker_config and surfaced on /dashboard/connect).
# Only set this explicitly if you want to choose your own value, or for
# shared/team deployments where rotating the token shouldn't lose anyone.
# To rotate later: wrangler secret put MCP_BEARER_TOKEN
MCP_BEARER_TOKEN=

# OPTIONAL — better-auth session signing secret. Only used if you enable
# the dashboard sign-in flow (Google OAuth) via the two GOOGLE_* fields
# below. Leave blank if you'll just use the MCP-bearer claim-on-first-
# visit dashboard auth (the default).
# To generate when needed: openssl rand -hex 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL — Google OAuth credentials for dashboard sign-in. Add these
# only if you want team members to sign into the dashboard with their
# Google accounts (instead of the single MCP-bearer claim flow). Set
# ALLOWED_AUTH_DOMAINS in wrangler.jsonc to restrict to your domain(s).
# Get from https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
